{"id":"h097","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Insulin was first isolated at the University of Edinburgh.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The University of Edinburgh has a strong medical research tradition and contributed to early 20th-century physiology.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-1.1417},{"text":"Insulin's discovery involved Scottish researcher J.J.R. Macleod, who was a professor in Scotland before moving to Canada.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-2.1416},{"text":"Macleod's Scottish connection explains why the claim seems plausible.","confidence":0.6,"lean":0.2,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-0.9042},{"text":"Insulin was first isolated in 1921–1922 at the University of Toronto by Banting and Best.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1126},{"text":"Banting and Best worked under Macleod's supervision, and James Collip contributed to purification.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-2.9632},{"text":"Macleod was based at Toronto when the work was done.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-2.9656},{"text":"The Edinburgh link is only Macleod's earlier career, not the site of isolation.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-2.8566},{"text":"The location of the isolation is a specific historical fact, documented as Toronto, not Edinburgh.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1186},{"text":"The claim that insulin was first isolated at Edinburgh is false.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1325}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":-0.4